 (269835,"sin (chata)","action","we and our fathers","sin","against God",GOD,"paired with iniquity and wickedness","v6: 'Both we and our fathers have SINNED (chata)' - the confession's thesis, the whole nation owning its guilt across the generations."),
 (269837,"commit iniquity (avah)","action","we and our fathers","commit iniquity","against God",GOD,"paired with sinning","v6: 'we have COMMITTED INIQUITY (avah)' - the twisting of the right, the second term of the threefold confession."),
 (269838,"do wickedness (rasha)","action","we and our fathers","do wickedness","against God",GOD,"paired with sinning","v6: 'we have DONE WICKEDNESS (rasha)' - the active wrong, the confession's full admission of guilt."),
