 (269694,"provoke (kaas)","action","the fathers","provoke to anger","the LORD by their deeds",GOD,"paired with the plague and Phinehas' intervention","v29: 'they PROVOKED (kaas) the LORD to anger with their deeds' - the rousing of God's wrath, met by plague."),
 (269707,"intervene (palal)","action","Phinehas","intervene / execute judgment","and the plague was stayed",GOD,"paired with the righteousness counted him","v30: 'Then Phinehas stood up and INTERVENED (palal), and the plague was stayed' - the zeal of Phinehas, decisive action that turned back the wrath."),
