 (307463,"spirit (ruach)","faculty","Moses","have the spirit embittered","by the people",IB,"paired with the bitterness and rash speech","v33: 'for they made his SPIRIT (ruach) bitter' - Moses' inner self soured by the people's strife, the meekest man goaded."),
 (307464,"bitter (marah)","state","Moses","be embittered","in spirit",IB,"paired with the spirit and rash words","v33: 'they made his spirit BITTER (marah)' - the embittering of Moses, provocation working inward."),
